WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.800
It all started with a panicked phone call.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:08.560
A local landlady who owned a downtown tenement&nbsp;
building had called the police in hysterics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:14.320
Something horrifying had happened to one of&nbsp;
her tenants; she couldn’t possibly explain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.600
The one detail she was able to articulate&nbsp;
was that his room “looked like a rainforest.”

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.960
A police response team was on the case in no&nbsp;
time. They drove down to the tenement building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.080
met the crying landlady at the door, and found&nbsp;
their way to the room that’d caused all this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:36.320
confusion. When they opened the door, they&nbsp;
saw with horror that she was right - trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:44.000
plants, fungi, and even insects and animals were&nbsp;
all over the room. It was teeming with life.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.080
The flora and fauna in this room didn’t&nbsp;
look like anything else on Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.120
And given the anomalous nature&nbsp;
of what had happened here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.880
it’s extremely possible they were right. The&nbsp;
tenant - a university professor who’d recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.800
gone on an anthropological expedition to the&nbsp;
Amazon rainforest - was nowhere to be seen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.440
But one of the officers spotted a grim&nbsp;
clue for what may have happened to him.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.880
A large colony of anomalous mold&nbsp;
was quickly growing on the far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.480
wall. The officer swore it was&nbsp;
a trick of the mind at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:22.160
but he was wrong. A human skull was sinking into&nbsp;
the tissue of the mold, and to make matters worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:28.560
whipping tendrils began to slither from the&nbsp;
empty eye sockets reaching for the new meat.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.600
Thankfully, for everyone who was still alive at&nbsp;
this point, the SCP Foundation swooped in and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.360
took over the situation with the help of a Mobile&nbsp;
Task Force and some containment specialists. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.640
landlady, the cops, and the other residents of&nbsp;
the building were given amnestics and relocated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.360
The building was purchased by the Foundation and&nbsp;
condemned while they searched the anomalous room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:54.800
for the source of this unchecked biological&nbsp;
growth. And they found their answer in a most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.960
unlikely form: An unmarked cassette tape,&nbsp;
still inside the player when they arrived.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:07.440
The recording on this cassette tape came to&nbsp;
be known as SCP-407. It may seem unassuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:13.120
when compared to immortal, misanthropic&nbsp;
lizard-monsters and multi-dimensional chaos gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:19.920
but the tape in that room, if it fell into&nbsp;
the wrong hands, could cause a mass ecological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:26.480
catastrophe that would inevitably bloom into&nbsp;
a dreaded XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:32.480
So, first thing’s first: What’s actually on this&nbsp;
tape? Thanks to brief samples heard in tests with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:37.760
D-Class Personnel, The Foundation was able to&nbsp;
discover that it was an approximately 28 minute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.720
long recording of a song. It’s performed&nbsp;
in an unknown language, and appears to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:48.000
sung acapella style by a group of unknown&nbsp;
individuals. Fearing potential degradation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.160
of the cassette tape, the Foundation backed it up&nbsp;
as an audio file in the Site 19 Computer Database.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.320
Those who’ve been able to listen to the song&nbsp;
during testing have had an overwhelmingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.840
positive emotional response - describing it&nbsp;
as 'soothing', 'glorious', and 'beautiful'.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.360
And for the first minute of its runtime, the&nbsp;
song’s anomalous effects really live up to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:15.920
reputation. When the song is played, it massively&nbsp;
accelerates cell growth within its auditory range.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.240
Its potency is increased by the volume&nbsp;
and the length it’s allowed to play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.680
It’s important to note that plugging&nbsp;
or covering your ears won’t make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:29.840
any difference. The area of effect seems to be&nbsp;
defined by how far the sound vibrations travel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.880
and whether you’re actually&nbsp;
able to hear it is irrelevant.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:37.680
But if you’re only listening for a minute or less,&nbsp;
you’ll be glad to feel the anomalous effects of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:44.880
being within SCP-407’s auditory range. During&nbsp;
this specific period of time, it’s been shown to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:51.760
be a kind of miracle-cure to almost all physical&nbsp;
maladies, with the exception of cancer. Thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:57.200
the cell growing and rejuvenating properties of&nbsp;
the song, the Foundation discovered that 407 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:03.040
an effective treatment for Alzheimer's disease,&nbsp;
Crohn's disease, brain and spinal cord injuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.000
and normally fatal infections or wounds,&nbsp;
amongst other maladies. It was like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.640
version of SCP-500 - the pills that cure&nbsp;
everything - but one that would never run out.&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.240
So, if it’s such an effective healer, why wasn’t&nbsp;
it more widely employed by the Foundation?

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.080
Because of what happens if you keep listening.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:28.000
If the song was played for two to three&nbsp;
minutes, the subject would begin to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:33.520
experience unnecessary and unchecked cell&nbsp;
growth - particularly on the skin. The result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:39.120
would mostly be benign tumors and calcium and&nbsp;
fat deposits, which though sometimes painful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.720
and disfiguring, are not life threatening. At&nbsp;
minute four, single celled organisms in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:51.120
auditory vicinity of the song begin to experience&nbsp;
accelerated mitosis, also known as cell division.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:55.120
This results in bacterial and fungal&nbsp;
growth that becomes extremely dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:02.400
for anyone and anything exposed. And beyond&nbsp;
minute five, things become truly monstrous.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.280
The Foundation only ever conducted two&nbsp;
tests wherein the song was fully played.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.640
These tests presented such a huge danger&nbsp;
that further testing of 407 was forbidden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:16.320
without explicit permission&nbsp;
from a member of O5 Command.&nbsp;

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:21.600
The first test involved a female member of D-Class&nbsp;
Personnel in a soundproofed but unsterilized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.760
testing chamber. As expected, she was initially&nbsp;
delighted by the music. It cured her injured knee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:33.600
and brought her back to a state of peak physical&nbsp;
fitness. But this didn’t last for long. She soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:39.520
began to report intense dizziness and stomach&nbsp;
pain, resulting in severe sickness. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:44.720
anomalous plant growth began in the corners of&nbsp;
the testing chamber. It seemed as though a whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:50.000
ecosystem was coming to life and evolving&nbsp;
at an impossible fast rate in the chamber.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.440
Over the next few minutes, the D-Class&nbsp;
experienced a nightmarish physical transformation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.440 --> 00:06:00.560
Her skin became a thick, callused mass.&nbsp;
She soon devolved further into a thick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:06.880
immobile blob of pure flesh, unrecognizable&nbsp;
as anything human while the chamber around her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:13.280
was becoming a lush rainforest of alien plants.&nbsp;
These plants grew around and eventually on her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.480
until there was nothing left. Shortly&nbsp;
after, all the plants died and decomposed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:23.440
giving away to a huge mound of anomalous&nbsp;
mold devouring the resulting mulch.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:29.040
The mold itself began to evolve, growing large&nbsp;
mouth and hand-like structures that it used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:35.120
feed itself on the surrounding flora and fauna&nbsp;
as it began to grow back. When the song ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.720
the Foundation brought the test to&nbsp;
a close, sterilized the room and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:44.880
collected some samples for later. There was&nbsp;
nothing left of the original D-Class subject.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:50.560
The second test wasn’t any nicer. While at first,&nbsp;
the subject - this time a male member of D-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:55.680
personnel - appeared to become more youthful&nbsp;
and even gain an inch of height, as the minutes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:01.920
passed, he began to experience extreme discomfort.&nbsp;
He soon began to vomit - with the vomit quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:07.120
blooming into plants. Plant shoots also began&nbsp;
to quickly spring out of his eyes and mouth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:12.560
until his entire body was destroyed by what&nbsp;
appeared to be a banana tree suddenly growing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:19.760
out of it. Once again, the testing chamber became&nbsp;
a whole ecosystem - this one filled with unique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:24.720
never before seen mammals. However, it all&nbsp;
came to an end when the room was taken over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:31.600
by a fast-growing, parasitic fungus that consumed&nbsp;
everything else with its spores and fungal stalks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.240
And it looked like it was breathing.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.880
There was something concerning about both of&nbsp;
these tests - beyond the obvious physical horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:44.640
of watching death-by-unchecked-cell-growth. What&nbsp;
was this mysterious fungus that kept appearing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.720
and seemed to take over everything it&nbsp;
touched in the end? The Foundation tested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.520
the samples it collected rigorously,&nbsp;
and came to a surprising conclusion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:59.120
They’d actually encountered this same&nbsp;
fungus before, but not in this dimension.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:06.400
SCP-507 is a man with dimension-hopping abilities.&nbsp;
The one problem is, he can’t control where and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:12.080
when he hops. As a result, he’s been stuck&nbsp;
in a number of scary alternate dimensions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:18.560
but one seemed eerily similar to what the&nbsp;
Foundation was encountering with SCP-407. In one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:24.880
dimension he briefly hopped into, 507 encountered&nbsp;
an abandoned version of Site 19, strewn with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:31.120
corpses covered in that same breathing mold. He&nbsp;
was horrified, but decided to inspect further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.080
hoping to find his way out of the facility and&nbsp;
discover some answers about what happened here.&nbsp;

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:42.000
However, when he found his way out, what he&nbsp;
discovered didn’t comfort him. The entire world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:48.640
seemed to be covered by this same mold. There&nbsp;
was nothing left. It’d consumed everything.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:52.240
Thanks to Foundation tests, both&nbsp;
molds were found to be similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:57.280
the Cordyceps Fungi - a kind of dangerous,&nbsp;
parasitic mold. Except this one appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:01.280
to be a far more evolved and even&nbsp;
more deadly version of the fungus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.080
What could this mean? What was the origin&nbsp;
of this anomalous song? Would it and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:10.880
fungus it seems to inspire someday destroy&nbsp;
the world as we know it, and kill us all?

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:16.400
We’ll never actually know the answer to any of&nbsp;
this, and it’s thanks to an extremely unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:23.040
ally: A Person of Interest nicknamed L.S.,&nbsp;
a prominent member of The Serpent’s Hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:29.120
This enigmatic figure had previously come into&nbsp;
possession of SCP-268 - a hat that made them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:35.440
almost impossible to detect. With the help of this&nbsp;
hat, L.S. breached Site 19 in an incident that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:41.040
later dubbed Security Breach Incident X23.
While it’s believed that L.S. mainly broke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.800
into the facility to make use of SCP-914,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.600
they performed a curious action along the&nbsp;
way: They hacked into the Foundation database,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:55.520
and deleted all traces of SCP-407,&nbsp;
effectively neutralizing it.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:01.360
In a note left by L.S., they said “You’ll&nbsp;
thank me for deleting what you call ‘407’.”

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:06.080
Why would a member of The Serpent’s Hand,&nbsp;
a Group of Interest that is often militant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:11.040
in their anti-neutralization stance,&nbsp;
neutralize an SCP themselves?

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:17.120
The answer to this lays in who exactly L.S.&nbsp;
Is. This mysterious figure isn’t technically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:22.960
one person - they’re a group of the same&nbsp;
person, namely a woman named Alison Chao,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.760
from a number of different dimensions.&nbsp;
They meet in the Wanderer’s Library,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:33.600
the headquarters of The Serpent’s Hand that exists&nbsp;
between dimensions, to coordinate their missions.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:39.600
Why does this matter in regards to SCP-407?&nbsp;
Because the nature of L.S. allows them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:44.880
know what’s going on in a huge number&nbsp;
of dimensions at once. This means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:52.640
much like the brief glimpse given by SCP-507,&nbsp;
L.S. likely knows about another universe where 407&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:58.720
and its horrific mold has already caused an&nbsp;
XK - Class Scenario and destroyed the world.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.120
And if it happened there due to poor&nbsp;
biological containment measures or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:10.320
407 falling into the wrong hands, it could happen&nbsp;
here too. Unless, of course, someone stepped in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:15.600
and dealt with the problem personally. And while&nbsp;
the Foundation’s policy is typically to contain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:20.640
rather than neutralize the anomalies they&nbsp;
find, we have to admit, we’re probably with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:28.240
the Serpent’s Hand on this one. Some songs, as&nbsp;
it turns out, are just better left unplayed...

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:37.200
Now go watch “SCP - 073 &amp; 076 - Cain Vs Able”&nbsp;
and “SCP - 5031 - Yet Another Murder Monster”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:42.640
to absorb even more knowledge about the&nbsp;
beings contained by the SCP Foundation.

